l of Bogotá** (Ruling Dec-18-2023), set an immovable precedent denying provisional measures to suspend inaugurations, empirically proving that local justice refuses to stop the fraud in any department. Additionally, the file of the massive presidential \"Tutelatón\" (**2026-00514-00**) was ruled against on July 3, 2026, and sent to the Council of State on July 14, making a second-instance ruling before the August 7 inauguration procedurally impossible."}
